Create a complete TypeScript module exporting a `Label` class and `generateLabels` function:

```typescript
export class Label {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly name: string;
  constructor(id: string, name: string);
}
export function generateLabels(names: readonly string[]): Label[];
```

Process names in input order without mutating the input. Trim each name; if a trimmed name is empty, throw `TypeError` before returning any result. Preserve the trimmed spelling in `Label.name`. Build the base identifier by lowercasing the trimmed name, replacing each run of non-ASCII-alphanumeric characters with `-`, and removing leading or trailing hyphens. If this produces an empty identifier, use `label`. Identifiers must be unique in output order: the first occurrence of a base uses the base itself, and later occurrences use `-2`, `-3`, and so on. Collisions are determined by the generated base, even when the original names differ. An empty input returns a new empty array.

